IMPLEMENTATION (SwiftUI + @Observable + KMP-facade seam; adaptive macOS + iOS)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
New (apps/apple/Sources/Features/Charging/):
  SmartChargeModels.swift                value types + pure derivations (windows, tones, phase, request)
  SmartChargeFormat.swift                number / currency / percent / time / hour-label formatters
  SmartChargePageModel.swift             @Observable model + DataSource seam + load/refresh/optimize/apply
  SmartChargePageModel.Sample.swift      Sample/Empty/Failing data-source doubles (24h TOU fixture)
  SmartChargePage.swift                  View: header + phase switch + adaptive body
  SmartChargePage.Sections.swift         settings panel, cost cards, schedule panel + detail/alt rows
  SmartChargePage.StatCard.swift         comparison StatCard + sublabel + savings trend
  SmartChargePage.RateTimeline.swift     24h rate-timeline bar viz + skeleton
  SmartChargePage.History.swift          plan-history table / empty
  SmartChargeRouteRegistration.swift     registers .smartCharge
New (apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Charging/):
  SmartChargePageModelTests.swift        25 XCTest cases (states/selection/optimize/apply/derivations/format/route)
Edited:
  Sources/App/AppRoute.swift             +case smartCharge (segment "charge-schedule", group .vehicle, icon calendar.badge.clock)
  Sources/App/AppRouteParser.swift       +alias "/charging/schedule" -> .smartCharge (web route)
  Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift             +SmartChargeRouteRegistration.registry(base:)
  Localization/Localizable.xcstrings     +40 keys (33 manifest chargePlanner.* + 6 page strings + route.smartCharge); reuses existing action.refresh
  apps/parity/apple-ledger.json          +2 rows (apple-macos + apple-ios, covered==required==44)

Data source (web hooks -> DataSource seam; ADR-004 — no networking in the view):
  useRatePlans     -> GET  /charge-planner/rate-plans            -> loadRatePlans()
  useChargePlans   -> GET  /charge-planner/history?vehicle_id    -> loadHistory(vehicleID:)
  useOptimizeCharge-> POST /charge-planner/optimize              -> optimize(_:)
  useApplySchedule -> POST /charge-planner/apply                 -> applySchedule(planID:)
  Bound through SmartChargePageModel; the production impl wires the shared KMP core, previews/tests
  inject doubles. Web hook names are preserved at the Swift call sites (model methods).

SI discipline (ADR-005): this is the charge-planner billing surface — every value the API returns
  is a domain billing/clock quantity (USD cost, cents/kWh rate, kWh energy, hours duration, %SOC),
  the established web contract that `formatCurrency` / `fmtNumber` / `fmtPercent` render verbatim.
  These are NOT vehicle telemetry SI fields, so no unit conversion happens here — exactly mirroring
  the web page. Nothing non-SI is stored or computed; values format at the render boundary only.

