PRE-EXISTING ENVIRONMENT ISOLATION (full disclosure — NOT this change; NOT red-as-green)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-existing, out-of-scope files are UNMODIFIED by this change (verified via
`git status --porcelain`) and outside this artifact's allowed files. They fail to compile on a
clean tree under the available newer Xcode 26.5 / Swift 6.3 front-end (the repo's macOS
verification is documented PENDING in apps/macos-pending-verifications.md):

  1) apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/Input.Previews.swift
     result-builder `return` diagnostics inside `#Preview` blocks. Isolated for BOTH the app and
     test actions via the command-line build setting EXCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES (a build override,
     no source edits). The macOS app + iOS app build clean with it isolated (above).
  2) apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift  (main-actor isolation), and
  3) apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Analytics/TimelinePageModelTests.swift (utcDayKey main-actor isolation).
     These are PRE-EXISTING broken XCTest files in the monolithic test bundle. To run THIS page's
     tests without editing out-of-scope files, the test invocation compiled ONLY this page's test
     file into the bundle via INCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES="SmartChargePageModelTests.swift" +
     EXCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES="*Tests.swift Input.Previews.swift" (a build override, no source
     edits). With that scoping the bundle builds and this page's 25 tests pass (above). No
     SmartCharge / AppRoute / AppRouteParser / TeslaSyncApp file produced any diagnostic.

Code signing was disabled (CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO) because no development certificate exists on
